WEBVTT

00:00.880 --> 00:07.920
There’s a $2 trillion social welfare and climate package,
is what it’s being called.

00:07.920 --> 00:13.160
Well, part of that is going to be about social welfare,
“human infrastructure,” as it’s being termed.

00:13.160 --> 00:16.200
It might be paying people to stay home.

00:16.200 --> 00:25.280
Does that upset an already fragile labor market right now,
where we have so many people not in the labor force?

00:25.280 --> 00:33.800
Agriculture in particular, we really struggle because we pay so much
in that lower, unskilled labor pool.

00:33.800 --> 00:39.840
And what if those people that are getting 20-plus-percent pay raises
get another 20% in 2022?

00:39.840 --> 00:42.500
Or what if they don’t even show up?

00:42.500 --> 00:45.900
That sign right there is from July.
I was on my way to Wisconsin to do a speaking engagement.

00:45.900 --> 00:50.040
I pulled into Culver’s. You guys don’t have Culver’s out here.
Maybe you do. I don’t know.

00:50.040 --> 00:53.460
I pulled in to get me a ButterBurger and to take a pee.
What’d that sign say?

00:53.460 --> 00:58.560
“Due to being short-staffed, our dining room will be closed for the day.
Drive-through is open.”

00:58.560 --> 01:01.220
You know how mad the Culver’s manager gets
when you pee in their drive-through?

01:04.220 --> 01:04.640
Okay.
